{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 31, :comments ["<b>Let the menorah be made.</b> One needs to know why it was necessary to say ״תֵּיעָשֶׂה הַמְּנוֹרָה״, and in the chapter HaKometz Rabah (Menachot 28a) they expounded ״תֵּיעָשֶׂה״ to include the other metals. And according to this, the verse was precise in saying ״תֵּיעָשֶׂה״ and not ״תַּעֲשֶׂה״, for in the days of Moses there was no need for this, since they made it of gold, and in the wilderness they had no need to make another."], :book :exodus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:33:29.311077247Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}